 # Local AI Workspace for Android
 
 An Android-first, offline-by-default AI workspace with a runtime-neutral Model Manager. The app keeps projects, chats, imported documents, local retrieval evidence, memory and model metadata in an on-device Room database. Model binaries stay in app-private storage; they are never stored in Room.
+
+Version **0.1.10** reorganizes Workspace around **Start chat** and optional **Start project**. Standalone chats and projects have separate lists and confirmed deletion; projects can contain multiple independently addressed chats and shared files/memory. Delete project removes its card and all owned chats/private documents/indexes/embeddings/project memory; deleting one project chat keeps its siblings and shared resources. Installed models and global memory remain. Existing projects are preserved by Room2→3 migration; deleted Personal workspace is no longer recreated at startup. Private-file cleanup has a durable retry outbox. [Behavior and phone checks](docs/WORKSPACE_010.md).
+
+Validation:129app tests executed/PASS,2unchanged compatibility tests up to date; debug assembly PASS; lint0errors/73existing warnings. Actual Android UI/native deletion checks **NOT_EXECUTED**. LiteRT0.1.9 warm-engine lifecycle is retained, with no SDK/model/sampler/quality/performance change. [0.1.10 artifact manifest](docs/validation/apk-010.json).
+
+[Download 0.1.10 APK from Drive](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DnJoNPZNrboP5QMgNXCkZxN1BcYP1wnI/view?usp=drivesdk) (91.54MB / 87.29MiB, ARM64, versionCode11). Install as an update to keep existing records. Release/signature/Drive metadata checks PASS; private sharing unchanged.
+
+## Previous release — 0.1.9
 
 Version **0.1.9** retains an unchanged healthy LiteRT CPU engine across chats/projects and creates a clean conversation for each new chat owner. Navigation no longer unconditionally unloads model weights. Idle engines expire after 10 minutes or reported idle memory pressure; Android may reclaim them earlier. Initial cold loading, changed configurations and CPU decoding still take time. GGUF retains its existing safe unload path. Chat deletion, private storage and Room schema2 remain. [Implementation and exact phone checks](docs/WARM_MODEL_019.md).
 
